"""cilctl: lease VMs from a CIL instance. Python 3.9+, standard library
only; runs on Linux, macOS and Windows (py -3 cilctl, or cilctl.cmd).

  cilctl [--cil NAME] [--url URL] [--jump HOPS] <command> ...

  cils                      the configured CIL profiles; * = selected
  setups                    the configured setup recipes
  health | pools | hosts | images
  leases [--all]            live leases (queued to expiring); --all: every one
  request <requester> [image] [cpu] [ram_mb] [disk_gb] [ttl_min] [npus]
  wait <id>                 poll until ready; store the key (dropped if
                            the lease has failed or is released)
  up [--name SLUG] [--image I] [--cpu N] [--ram MB] [--disk GB]
     [--ttl MIN] [--npus N] [--setup RECIPE]
                            request + wait (+ setup); prints how to connect
  setup <id> RECIPE         llama-server with a model, plus OpenCode
  ssh <id> [cmd...]         shell, or one command (one argument is a
                            shell line); ~/.opencode/bin is on PATH
  opencode <id> [dir]       OpenCode TUI in the lease
  forward <id> [local_port] [remote_port]
                            forward 127.0.0.1:local_port to the lease's
                            127.0.0.1:remote_port (default 8080 8080)
  copy|scp <id> SRC... DST  copy up or down; lease paths start with ':'
  apt <id>                  optional: point the guest's apt at the CIL mirror
  extend <id> <min>
  events <id>
  release <id>              delete, wait for released, drop the key
  doctor [id]               which route reaches the API and the lease

The CIL is --url, else $CILCTL_URL, else the url of the selected profile
(--cil, $CILCTL_CIL, or the config's default). Profiles and setup recipes
live in $CILCTL_CONFIG (default ~/.config/cilctl/config.toml); see the
README. The jump hops (user@host[:port],...) are --jump, else
$CILCTL_JUMP, else the profile's; "none" turns them off.

Lease responses carry the VM's private ssh key: they are parsed here and
only allowlisted fields are printed. Keys live in
$CILCTL_STATE/<profile>/<id>/key (default ~/.cache/cilctl; 0600, an
owner-only ACL on Windows) and are deleted on release.

Environment: CILCTL_URL, CILCTL_CIL, CILCTL_JUMP, CILCTL_POOL,
CILCTL_CONFIG, CILCTL_STATE, CILCTL_SSH and CILCTL_SCP (client binaries).
"""
